.TH RUN-DOMAINS 1 "2026-10-12" "cti-agent 1.3" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
run-domains \- weekly domains check: run cti-domains, then mail the report to the domains audience
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B run\-domains
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.PP
.B sudo cti\-agent run\-domains
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B run-domains
runs
.BR cti\-domains (1)
over the domain inventory and mails the result through
.BR cti\-mailer (1)
.BR "\-\-lane dom" .
No model is involved: every line of the report is a DNS answer, an HTTP
response, a certificate or a registrar field.
.PP
It is run by
.B cti\-agent\-domains.service
from
.B cti\-agent\-domains.timer
every Monday at 08:00
.RB ( Persistent=true ),
after the weekly rollup and the AppSec report. The unit runs as
.BR ctiagent ,
with
.B cti\-agent\-alert@.service
on failure.
.PP
The steps, in order:
.TP
.B 1. Prepare
Checks that
.I $FLEET_CODE/bin/cti\-domains
and
.I $FLEET_CODE/bin/cti\-mailer
are executable (fatal if not), sets
.I $FLEET_HOME/state
to 0700, creates today's HTML, text, CSV and actions files empty at 0600, and
deletes today's subject file so a stale one cannot be mistaken for this
run's.
.TP
.B 2. Check
.B cti\-domains \-\-out \-\-text\-out \-\-subject\-out \-\-csv\-out
probes every domain and writes all four files, comparing with last week's
state and then replacing it. Fatal on a non-zero exit.
.TP
.B 3. Subject
The first line of the subject file. Fatal, and nothing is sent, if the
file is missing, empty, or its first line is blank.
.TP
.B 4. Send
.B cti\-mailer \-\-lane dom
with the HTML, text and subject and the CSV attached, plus
.B \-\-dry\-run
on a dry run. The lane resolves
.B DOM_TO
against
.B DOM_ALLOW_TO
and refuses if either is unset; there is no fallback to the digest audience.
Fatal on failure.
.TP
.B 5. Lock-down ticket
.B cti\-jira \-\-domains\-actions
with the day's actions file and
.BR \-\-for\-real :
one Jira ticket for IT listing the DNS changes, or a comment on the one
already open when the list has changed (see
.BR cti\-jira (1)).
After the send, and never fatal: a Jira failure is logged and the run still
succeeds. On a dry run it runs without
.B \-\-for\-real
and only prints the ticket it would file.
.PP
A dry run passes
.B \-\-no\-state\-write
to
.BR cti\-domains ,
so it still probes every domain and queries the registrar, and overwrites
today's report files, but leaves last week's baseline in place: the real run
still reports this week's changes. It sends nothing.
.SH OPTIONS
A single shell argument.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Probe, render and print the subject; do not send and do not advance the
baseline.
.PP
Anything else, or more than one argument, is refused with exit status 1.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.I fleet.env
is sourced with every assignment exported, and its values replace the
process environment, except
.B FLEET_HOME
and
.BR FLEET_CODE ,
which keep the value the unit or wrapper injected.
.B cti\-domains
loads it again itself.
.TP
.B FLEET_HOME
State directory.
Default:\~\fB$HOME\fR (not \fI$HOME/fleet\fR); the unit sets
\fI/var/lib/cti\-agent\fR.
.TP
.B FLEET_CODE
Code directory.
Default:\~\fB$FLEET_HOME\fR; the unit sets \fI/opt/cti\-agent\fR.
.TP
.B FLEET_ENV
The config file.
Default:\~\fI$FLEET_HOME/fleet.env\fR.
.TP
.BR DOM_TO ", " DOM_ALLOW_TO
The audience and its allowlist, read by
.B cti\-mailer
(section 4, "the weekly domains check"). No fallback.
.PP
.BR DOMAINS_FILE ,
.B GODADDY_PAT
and the
.B DOMAINS_*
probe settings are read by
.BR cti\-domains (1).
.SH FILES
Under
.IR /var/lib/cti\-agent/state ,
directory mode 0700.
.I DATE
is the UTC date.
.TP
.IR domains\-DATE.html ", " domains\-DATE.txt ", " domains\-DATE.csv
The report and the per-host CSV, 0600. A second run on the same day
replaces them.
.TP
.I domains\-DATE\-actions.json
The DNS changes for IT, written by
.B cti\-domains \-\-actions\-out
and read by
.BR "cti\-jira \-\-domains\-actions" ,
0600.
.TP
.I domains\-DATE.subject
The subject line, written by
.BR cti\-domains .
.TP
.I domains\-state.json
Last week's observations; replaced by a real run, untouched by a dry run.
.TP
.I /etc/cti\-agent/domains.txt
The inventory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The report was sent (or rendered, on a dry run).
.TP
.B 1
An unknown or extra argument;
.B cti\-domains
or
.B cti\-mailer
is missing;
.B cti\-domains
failed (often an inventory the service account cannot read); no subject; or
the send failed, including the mailer's refusal when
.B DOM_TO
or
.B DOM_ALLOW_TO
is unset.
.SH EXAMPLES
Preview this week's report without sending or moving the baseline:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent run\-domains \-\-dry\-run
sudo less /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/domains\-$(date \-u +%F).txt
.EE
.PP
Send it now instead of waiting for Monday:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent run\-domains
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cti\-domains (1),
.BR cti\-mailer (1),
.BR cti\-agent (1)
.PP
RUNBOOK.md section 11g; fleet\-kit/README.md, "The weekly domains check".
